CORE broken-cprover-smt-backend
main.c
--unwind 43 --unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ read through a pointer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ read as a member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ pointer member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ loop: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\[main\.unwind\.\d+\]
--
A union read as a whole was represented by the fields of its widest member.
Copies of the union, and reads of a member of a union that is a member of a
struct, or through a pointer to the member's type, then took the other
members' values from those fields: a reinterpretation of a floating-point
number, which lost the constant stored as an int (so the loop bound became
symbolic) and the target of the pointer (a spurious failure of "pointer
member").
